<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Cook</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1728">1728</a>–<a href="/years/1779">1779</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Captain Cook</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Cook was a British naval officer who led three voyages of exploration in the Pacific between 1768 and 1779. He charted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, visited Tahiti and the Society Islands, named New Caledonia in 1774 and reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a> in 1778. He was killed in a clash at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kealakekua-bay">Kealakekua Bay</a> on Hawaii Island in February 1779.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-cook.jpg" alt="James Cook" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nathaniel Dance-Holland · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Captainjamescookportrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
